What is Nicergoline API?
Nicergoline API (Active Pharmaceutical Ingredient) is the primary raw material used in the production of nicergoline-based pharmaceutical formulations. Nicergoline, a semisynthetic ergot derivative, is widely utilized in the treatment of cognitive disorders, particularly in elderly patients suffering from vascular dementia, Alzheimer’s disease, and other cerebral insufficiencies. The API form is typically produced in bulk and later processed into various pharmaceutical dosage forms such as tablets, capsules, and injections. It functions by enhancing cerebral blood flow and exhibits neuroprotective, antioxidant, and anti-platelet aggregation properties, making it valuable in the therapeutic landscape of neurodegenerative diseases.

Marketed under various brand names globally, Nicergoline is administered orally and via injections. It is approved for use in multiple countries across Europe, Asia, and Latin America, positioning it as a key therapeutic agent in managing cognitive decline and peripheral vascular diseases.

